784
01:02:15,107 --> 01:02:21,911
So, I'm sure you are all familiar with after 48, sometimes just referred to as the zoning act.

785
01:02:23,122 --> 01:02:27,725
It has a long history in Massachusetts law, just for a bit of background it dates back to the 1920s.

786
01:02:27,805 --> 01:02:34,209
It was codified as Chapter 48 in 1954 and then there was a major revision to the act.

787
01:02:35,554 --> 01:02:38,937
1975 that really gave us the modern version that we see today.

788
01:02:38,957 --> 01:02:44,821
And there have been changes since then from time to time, but it really formed what we look at today.

789
01:02:44,841 --> 01:03:00,253
And often when we're doing research and looking at cases, at least I know I keep an eye out for kind of the pre-1975 cases versus the post-1975 cases, because there are some differences and sometimes you just want to make sure that what you're relying on still works under the new act.

790
01:03:01,294 --> 01:03:04,797
So we'll talk a little bit now about the purposes of the act.

791
01:03:05,536 --> 01:03:18,222
I'm sure a lot of you are familiar with this, but I figured I'd just kind of cover the basics that the purposes of the act, the purposes of zoning are to give us consistent statewide frameworks for regulating land uses.

792
01:03:18,702 --> 01:03:32,348
And zoning encourages the adoption of modern ordinances and compliance with the constitution to provide standards and procedures to administer local zoning and to give communities the ability to

793
01:03:33,482 --> 01:03:42,008
work at a local level to preserve character and encourage land uses the way that the city, the policy makers in the city find most appropriate.

794
01:03:42,729 --> 01:03:48,973
Major purposes of zoning are, as you all know, health, safety, public convenience.

795
01:03:51,835 --> 01:04:00,402
So the way the goals of zoning are achieved is through having uniform districts with specific boundaries,

796
01:04:01,863 --> 01:04:12,630
specific and clear uses of lands and structures in each of those districts, clear dimensional requirements, and then conditions under which different uses may be permitted.

797
01:04:12,750 --> 01:04:27,040
And this is really important, and I know it's really important to your board as well, because when people try to do projects or come forward or look at your ordinances, they want to be able to clearly understand what they can and can't do and what types of uses may need relief and such things.

798
01:04:27,080 --> 01:04:30,162
So being as clear as possible is important.

799
01:04:33,367 --> 01:04:49,853
So administering the act, adoption of a zoning ordinance, when you adopt obviously your zoning ordinances, and then they will specify the types of permits that can be used and who grants them.

800
01:04:50,193 --> 01:05:01,997
And so one thing that's a little different in cities than in most towns is that, and it is common in Medford as well, is that your city council under the ordinance has special permit granting authorities, which we sometimes see in cities

801
01:05:02,502 --> 01:05:15,133
It's more rare to see, at least in my experience, slack boards have special permit granting authorities it's usually vested with planning boards and Board of Appeals in town, but not uncommon in cities, and Medford is right in line with that.

802
01:05:16,654 --> 01:05:18,176
So, on this slide.

803
01:05:19,060 --> 01:05:34,432
Administering the act and I do have an asterisk at the top and there are a couple items that are asterisk because they are things that are technically outside of the zoning act, but that sometimes are under the purview of the zoning board so I just wanted to keep them in there, so that you know folks are generally aware of them.

804
01:05:35,260 --> 01:05:37,160
Zoning Board of Appeals grant variances.

805
01:05:38,101 --> 01:05:44,622
