1089
01:38:06,238 --> 01:38:08,699
So there's no question later what somebody was supposed to do

1090
01:38:09,539 --> 01:38:36,778
for their project and it's always good to reference the plans and the decision and then make sure they're filed somewhere you know with a copy of the decision where people can find them you know if it's years down the road things are probably getting a little easier with digital copies but definitely you want to be able to find that plan later if there's a question about something so one other comment you know the board can't delegate its discretionary authority and so you have to keep that in mind with conditions that

1091
01:38:37,270 --> 01:38:51,500
You don't want to condition something kind of, you know, too far down the road where, you know, saying, you know that a building commissioner or staff or somebody in the town might be responsible for something that's really part of the boards discretionary authority.

