1127
01:42:20,205 --> 01:42:24,908
So required findings for granting variances, the statute has three findings.

1128
01:42:24,988 --> 01:42:37,214
The first one is that you have to find that there are unique land conditions relating to soil shape, topography of the land or the structure, which affect that land or structure, but not generally the zoning district.

1129
01:42:37,294 --> 01:42:39,115
So that could be something like ledge,

1130
01:42:39,797 --> 01:43:02,431
that could be something like an unusual existing structure that maybe takes up, you know, most of the property and that's not common in the neighborhood, wetlands, but something about the property, you know, it has a particularly unique shape that makes it necessary that it needs relief and that also is unique, you know, it's not common to the whole neighborhood.

1131
01:43:03,157 --> 01:43:04,958
So that's the first finding.

1132
01:43:05,138 --> 01:43:09,842
And the second finding would be that a literal, oops, did it not click?

1133
01:43:09,902 --> 01:43:10,242
Hold on.

1134
01:43:11,783 --> 01:43:12,103
There we go.

1135
01:43:12,544 --> 01:43:18,808
That a literal enforcement of the ordinance would create a substantial hardship, financial otherwise to the applicant.

1136
01:43:19,028 --> 01:43:23,791
And I know the statute says financial, but there's a world of case law that says it can't just be financial.

1137
01:43:24,792 --> 01:43:30,056
And again, the hardship has to actually be related to whatever that soil condition is.

1138
01:43:30,116 --> 01:43:31,797
It actually has to be created by that.

1139
01:43:31,978 --> 01:43:44,270
So it has to be, you know, because we have this ledge all over the back of the property, you know, we can't meet this particular setback requirement or we can't meet this particular coverage requirement, they have to actually be tied together.

1140
01:43:45,578 --> 01:43:57,326
And then the third element of grant of variance is that you can grant that relief without substantial detriment to the public good and without modifying or substantially derogating from the intent and purpose of the award.

1141
01:43:57,707 --> 01:44:02,630
And that gives you an opportunity to analyze the impacts of the variance.

1142
01:44:05,533 --> 01:44:12,838
What it means to grant a variance, which I'm sure you're all familiar with, but that you're authorizing dimensional requirements that wouldn't otherwise be permitted.

1143
01:44:14,942 --> 01:44:19,604
you know, the burdens on the applicant to come in and prove that they need this variance.

1144
01:44:19,644 --> 01:44:22,026
And again, the hardship isn't, you know, alone isn't enough.

1145
01:44:22,086 --> 01:44:30,850
It's not just that I have a challenge, but that, um, you know, there really is some unique special condition of this land or of the structure that's creating that problem.

1146
01:44:31,391 --> 01:44:34,752
And that they can go ahead and do what they're proposing without causing that detriment.

1147
01:44:35,253 --> 01:44:37,294
Um, no one is entitled to a variance.

1148
01:44:38,214 --> 01:44:43,277
Um, you know, there's case law we've cited in here that variants just should be granted sparingly.

1149
01:44:43,888 --> 01:44:49,112
I will say, I think how courts evaluate variances often relates to the degree of your variance.

1150
01:44:49,573 --> 01:45:00,702
So if you're talking about, you know, a couple of feet on a lot area requirement, something more de minimis, it may be, you know, evaluated differently by a court.

1151
01:45:00,742 --> 01:45:12,572
And some of that has to do kind of with the detriment concept, as opposed to somebody who's looking for an extreme dimensional variance or use variances, which may get a higher kind of substantive review because they're more significant

1152
01:45:13,148 --> 01:45:13,794
variations.

1153
01:45:16,518 --> 01:45:23,984
So similar to special permits, variances have lapsing and extension provisions.

1154
01:45:24,424 --> 01:45:29,648
So variances need to be exercised within one year of the date of the grant of a lapse.

1155
01:45:30,549 --> 01:45:35,773
They can get a six month extension needs to be applied for before the lapse happens.

1156
01:45:36,534 --> 01:45:42,999
And there's a little bit of case law, but not a lot on what it means to exercise a variance.

1157
01:45:43,832 --> 01:45:58,867
The way I usually like to describe it is that you, you have to have changed your position in reliance on the variance, so there needs to be recorded the registry of deeds that's not enough to exercise it, you know, it would really be, did you pull a building permit and start work.

1158
01:45:59,358 --> 01:46:01,820
Did you sell the property to a bona fide purchaser?

1159
01:46:01,840 --> 01:46:03,241
Did you change your position?

1160
01:46:03,261 --> 01:46:05,623
Did somebody really rely on and use that variance?

1161
01:46:06,144 --> 01:46:12,329
And there is case law out there, but that is extremely fact specific area of the law.

1162
01:46:12,349 --> 01:46:15,792
So if that question comes up, by all means, let us know and we'll help with that.

1163
01:46:15,832 --> 01:46:20,716
But there's really only a handful of cases that deal with what it means to exercise a variance.

1164
01:46:22,157 --> 01:46:25,240
Attorney Stein, is that six month restriction

1165
