1208
01:49:01,615 --> 01:49:11,137
So that's an area that at some point might get decided by a higher court, but very little guidance on it, on it now, other than just the words of the statute and that one land court case.

1209
01:49:15,635 --> 01:49:26,510
So, again, variances can have conditions, they can pull you as the board can impose conditions and safeguards and limitations similar to.

1210
01:49:28,241 --> 01:49:35,386
the special permits, but the difference being that you can't tie it to the applicant or to renewal.

1211
01:49:35,486 --> 01:49:43,511
And conceptually, the difference with that really is that when you're granting a variance, you're actually varying the zoning for that property.

1212
01:49:43,571 --> 01:49:49,095
It's really tied to the property as opposed to a special permit that's more tied to the use of the property.

1213
01:49:49,575 --> 01:49:55,339
And so because the concept of variances is that you're really saying this is a property that only needs 20,000 square feet, not 25,

1214
01:49:56,539 --> 01:50:01,922
that's not something that you really would tie to a person, you know, or a particular project.

1215
01:50:02,002 --> 01:50:06,805
So it does have a conceptual basis to it, but it's really more that the variance is varying.

1216
01:50:07,085 --> 01:50:13,528
I'm going to shift gears a little bit and just talk about a couple other zoning concepts.

1217
01:50:15,050 --> 01:50:33,181
So accommodations for persons with disabilities, there is some language in chapter 48, section three, that talks about that local land use and health and safety laws, regulations, practices, ordinances, et cetera, obviously can't be applied in a discriminatory manner.

1218
01:50:33,861 --> 01:50:44,308
And, you know, some time to time you may get an application for say a variance or some other relief that's tied to the fact that somebody requires an accommodation, perhaps to put in a wheelchair ramp

1219
01:50:45,199 --> 01:50:46,440
other aspect of their home.

1220
01:50:46,500 --> 01:50:50,824
And so if you get questions about those, and you need help with that, let us know.

1221
01:50:50,844 --> 01:50:59,051
But I just wanted to flag that obviously, you know, in addition to just general discrimination laws also in the zoning act as well.

1222
01:50:59,551 --> 01:51:06,017
And then the Federal Fair Housing Act also will apply in zoning situations.

1223
01:51:06,217 --> 01:51:09,760
And so again, from time to time, you may get requests for accommodations, what have you.

1224
01:51:11,082 --> 01:51:15,645
You know, there is a kind of a framework to evaluate those, and we can help with those if they come up.

1225
01:51:18,167 --> 01:51:21,510
So, and just a little bit more guidance on those.

1226
01:51:22,691 --> 01:51:35,241
I don't really, so I need to read the slides, but, you know, the point is that you want to make sure that folks have equal opportunities to enjoy their homes, equal opportunities, you know, for the accommodations that they need.

1227
01:51:36,978 --> 01:51:40,881
and so that they have fair opportunities to live within the community as everybody else.

1228
01:51:40,921 --> 01:51:42,602
And that's really all we're trying to accomplish.

1229
01:51:43,263 --> 01:51:48,386
And so sometimes the analysis can get fact specific about accommodations and what have you.

1230
01:51:48,446 --> 01:51:51,909
But again, if those come up and you have questions, just let us know.

1231
01:51:52,769 --> 01:51:57,873
So I'm going to shift gears a little bit now out of zoning and into some of the general

1232
01:51:58,507 --> 01:52:03,069
Um, kind of open meeting law, public record concepts that just apply to all boards and commissions.

1233
01:52:03,109 --> 01:52:17,034
So I feel like it's always helpful to put those in our area specific analysis, but, um, the open meeting law, obviously your, um, meetings, the agendas need to be posted 48 hours in advance of the meeting that does exclude weekends and legal holidays.

1234
01:52:17,054 --> 01:52:25,017
So always kind of keep in mind when a, like a Monday holidays coming up that, um, you know, if you have a Tuesday meeting, it'll make sure you post the Thursday before things like that.

1235
01:52:26,589 --> 01:52:33,393
You need a quorum of the board to deliberate, and a quorum is a majority of the members in office.

1236
01:52:33,854 --> 01:52:43,440
It gets a little trickier in zoning sometimes because you still, for say, a special partner for variance, or you need a supermajority to act, right?

1237
01:52:43,460 --> 01:52:52,166
So you need more than, if it's a five-member board, you could have a meeting of three, but you still wouldn't be able to approve a variance, for example, because you need that fourth member.

1238
01:52:54,397 --> 01:53:10,195
So for public hearings the board has to have the same access to the meeting as the public or the public to the board, you know, this is honestly taken on a bit of a different meaning over the last couple years as we've started to get into the areas of hybrid meetings and remote meetings

1239
01:53:11,243 --> 01:53:29,172
What that means, but the bottom line is that you know their public meetings they, you know, especially when you have public hearings, folks need to be able to ask questions and interact and see plans and so you know we've spent a lot of time over the last couple years figuring out what that means in a remote and sometimes hybrid environment.

1240
01:53:29,707 --> 01:53:34,408
but it is important that the public has access.

1241
01:53:34,508 --> 01:53:42,910
Big one, maybe the only exclamation point in the presentation, obviously no deliberating over email or outside of a public meeting.

1242
01:53:43,450 --> 01:53:58,053
So, you can circulate a document that's gonna be discussed in a meeting, but nobody should be hitting reply all and sharing their comments or suggested changes or corrections or what have you via email.

1243
01:53:59,093 --> 01:54:02,295
You can do things like scheduling over email, because that's not a deliberation.

1244
01:54:02,836 --> 01:54:06,658
You can distribute the packets over email that are going to be used at the meeting.

1245
01:54:07,079 --> 01:54:13,683
But any back and forth, sharing of opinions and thoughts and things like that, not over email.

1246
01:54:13,703 --> 01:54:15,485
We have to save those for our public meetings.

1247
01:54:16,846 --> 01:54:21,829
So another aspect that comes up under the Open Meeting Law is questions about site visits.

1248
01:54:22,490 --> 01:54:26,392
So the Open Meeting Law actually says that on-site instructions are not meetings.

1249
01:54:26,412 --> 01:54:27,293
They have to be posted.

1250
01:54:28,235 --> 01:54:29,756
provided there's no deliberation.

1251
01:54:29,916 --> 01:54:31,777
So that's something important to keep in mind.

1252
01:54:31,837 --> 01:54:35,299
You don't have to post the meeting, but you can't be pointing things out.

1253
01:54:35,379 --> 01:54:41,262
And it's hard sometimes because you go and you see something or what have you, but you can't kind of have those conversations.

1254
01:54:41,943 --> 01:54:45,124
Sometimes boards will be inclined to say, well, let's post it just in case.

1255
01:54:46,005 --> 01:54:51,948
The one caveat with that is that the board doesn't have the ability to invite members of the public onto somebody's private property.

1256
01:54:52,327 --> 01:54:54,870
In fact, the board doesn't have the right to go on somebody's private property.

1257
01:54:54,910 --> 01:54:59,615
So if the property owner says, sure, I'll host a site visit, you just want to make sure, yep, they're inviting the board on.

1258
01:55:00,116 --> 01:55:03,459
And you can check with them and say, we'd like to post this so we can talk about things.

1259
01:55:03,759 --> 01:55:05,021
Is it OK if the public comes?

1260
01:55:05,101 --> 01:55:07,644
If they say no, then you can't.

1261
01:55:07,744 --> 01:55:10,467
And you just have to be careful not to have any of those deliberations.

1262
01:55:11,891 --> 01:55:15,699
And obviously in land use site visits can sometimes be very important.

1263
01:55:15,719 --> 01:55:22,893
It's often, you know, especially for big projects, it's really helpful to see the site and know what you're looking at, not just some of the paper plans.

